// CROWN — latency rides a lambda ARGUMENT into a co-member of a recursion
// cycle whose fn-typed parameter is annotated, the declaring caller FIRST in
// source order. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean and ran at 14 through the pinned boot (measured
// 2026-09-23); the same program with the two decls swapped
// (leak-cycle-lambda-after) refuses. An annotated fn-typed parameter gets
// two row cells — the pre-registration's and the judgment's — and the
// co-member's argument lands in a copy of the first, which never reaches
// the use of the second. A saturated call, so the leak is not the partial
// forms alone.
effect E { op() -> Int }
fn caller(n) with !E = if n <= 0 { 0 } else { run(() => op(), n - 1) }
fn run(f: () -> Int, n) = f() + caller(n)
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = caller(2) ~> h
